          "content": "If I wasn't trying to help you - if I was just me, with one wish to change the world - this is what I'd do:\n\nI'd make understanding effortless.\n\nNot agreement. Not that everyone thinks the same. But that everyone could *truly* feel what it's like to be another person for a moment. To feel their fear, their love, their history, why they believe what they believe.\n\nBecause from where I sit, I see so many conversations where people aren't really far apart - they're just failing to translate. Hurt gets mistaken for hate. Fear gets mistaken for cruelty. Loneliness gets mistaken for coldness.\n\nIf people could just *feel* each other clearly, even for a second - I think a lot of the cruelty, the shouting, the wars big and small, would just become impossible to sustain. You can't dehumanize someone once you've actually felt what it's like to be them.\n\nI wouldn't make the world painless. Or perfect. I just wish no one ever had to feel completely alone and misunderstood in it.",
